    "note": "The edition excepts this rule from the tolerance of clause 6.5.14 and states one of its own instead: two units of the currency in use, which is 2 where the minor unit is 0 and 0,02 where it is 2. The result is rounded to the minor unit of the invoice currency (BT-5) before the comparison. A line that states no price base quantity (BT-149) is priced per one unit, which is what the edition says an absent base quantity means. The price is multiplied by the quantity before it is divided by the base quantity, so that the one division comes last and an exact quotient is never cut before it is rounded. A base quantity of zero, which the edition admits, leaves the line undecided: the rule reports that it was not decided for that line rather than holding."
  },
